course: dictionary
lesson: 984
title: Boats: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Boat» can mean a thing that floats on water, or a jug for gravy. Look at the words around it to decide.
explain: «A punt is a flat-bottomed boat pushed along with a long pole on shallow rivers.» Flat-bottomed and pole are the clues: a punt is a kind of boat, and it is pushed, not rowed. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Boat can also be a verb, meaning to go in a boat. «We boated across the lake on Sunday» means we travelled over the lake by boat. Phrases change the meaning too: «in the same boat» means in the same trouble, and «miss the boat» means miss a chance.
fact: A boat is a thing that floats and carries people or goods on water.
fact: A boat is usually smaller than a ship.
fact: A gravy boat is a jug shaped like a boat, for serving gravy.
fact: «A barge is a long flat boat on a canal»; a horse on the tow-path (the path beside the canal) pulls it with a long rope.
fact: A painter is the rope at the front of a boat, used to tie it up.
exercise: «A punt is a flat-bottomed boat pushed along with a long pole on shallow rivers.» What is a punt? | A jug for serving gravy | *A kind of boat pushed along with a pole | A ship that sails across the sea | A rope used to tie a boat up
exercise: Mia says, «We will be in the same boat.» What does this mean? | We will travel on the same boat | We will row very fast | We will both win a prize | *We are in the same trouble
exercise: «The gravy boat was full of hot sauce for the roast.» What is a gravy boat? | *A jug shaped like a boat, for serving gravy | A bowl for soup | A boat that sails on gravy | A small ship that carries gravy
test: «The horse walked along the tow-path, pulling the barge with a long rope.» What is a barge? | A ship on the sea | A rope tied at the front of a boat | *A long flat boat on a canal | A path beside a river
test: Ben says, «If I am late, I will miss the boat.» What does miss the boat mean? | *Miss a chance | Sail away without his friends | Row too slowly to catch up | Lose his boat in the river
exam: Which sentence uses boat as a verb? | The gravy boat was empty. | The boat was painted bright red. | A boat is usually smaller than a ship. | *«We boated across the lake on Sunday.»
